    {
      "$type": "Models.Core.Folder, Models",
      "ShowInDocs": false,
      "GraphsPerPage": 6,
      "Name": "Simple Rotational Grazing Example",
      "ResourceName": null,
      "Children": [
        {
          "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
          "Text": "“Simple Rotational Grazing” is an example of a simple 5-paddock set-duration rotation. \n\nStock are bought (see the Manager component “BuyStock”) as the simulation initialises and they remain in the simulation for the duration (not continually bought and sold). This component has a user input of the desired whole-farm stocking rate. It scans the simulation for all the paddocks and sums their areas to give the area of the whole farm and then buys sufficient head of stock to achieve the user input of stocking rate. The user also sets the type of stock to buy.\n\nThe Manager component “TargetRotationLength” moves the stock between paddocks, optionally harvests unutilised herbage and also optionally feeds silage to the stock. \n\nThe scripts provide examples of:\n\n* setting several commonly-needed stock characteristics \n* buying stock\n* finding out the current location of the stock\n* changing the location of the stock\n* feeding supplements based on a range of criteria\n* harvesting excess biomass\n\n\n",
          "Name": "Simple Rotational Grazing Explained",
          "ResourceName": null,
          "Children": [],
          "Enabled": true,
          "ReadOnly": false
        },
        {
          "$type": "Models.Core.Simulation, Models",
          "Descriptors": null,
          "Name": "A Simple Rotational Grazing",
          "ResourceName": null,
          "Children": [
