            {
              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
              "Text": "These plots (working left to right and top to bottom) show:\r\n\r\n* The liveweight and condition score of the stock. By the end of the simulation the stock (Angus steers – see the BuyStock component) are reaching their mature liveweight and gains have levelled off. The blue shaded background shows the location of the stock at any time with different intensities of blue for different paddocks. Click and hold on the shading to see the location value.\r\n* The pasture intake (on a per head basis) and total intake. Total intake is greater than the pasture intake when there is silage supplementation.\r\n* The standing pasture biomass in each of the paddocks (the lines) with the head count of the stock as symbols. The decline in head count is because there are some deaths. The farm us under-stocked in the second year with paddocks accumulating high biomass values.\r\n* Growth rates in the paddocks and an accumulation of harvested silage\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "Name": "Memo1",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
